<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-WMC mine restarts after miner's death.</title>
<headline>RTRS-WMC mine restarts after miner's death.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>WMC Ltd said on Monday production restarted late on Friday at its Rocky's Reward nickel mine in Western Australia after being closed when a man was killed in a rockfall last Wednesday.</p>
<p>No production was lost, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>However, development work on new mining areas at the deposit remained suspended pending the conclusion of investigations into the death, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;We've got to be sure that there is nothing suspect about how we perform our investigation,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
